WEBVTT

00:03.580 --> 00:07.000
How will the end of the world
come upon us?

00:07.790 --> 00:09.590
It's something
that I've always wondered about

00:09.800 --> 00:10.710
since I was a kid.

00:11.460 --> 00:12.380
But go figure.

00:12.550 --> 00:13.930
The end arrived without warning,

00:14.550 --> 00:16.050
in a way that nobody
could have imagined.

00:17.680 --> 00:20.180
The whole thing started
roughly four years ago.

00:20.810 --> 00:22.270
That was when Dr. Skinner,

00:22.480 --> 00:23.390
a man touted

00:23.560 --> 00:25.520
as having the most brilliant mind
since Einstein,

00:25.690 --> 00:27.440
began to sell a miracle painkiller

00:27.650 --> 00:29.440
that he had developed
known as "Hapna".

00:30.230 --> 00:32.900
Since it was cheap
and had no side effects whatsoever,

00:33.070 --> 00:34.240
it dominated the market instantly,

00:34.860 --> 00:37.160
and the world became
a Hapna-filled wonderland.

00:38.120 --> 00:41.200
It liberated people
from all kinds of suffering

00:41.410 --> 00:44.040
and was even celebrated
as "the drug that saved the world".

00:44.910 --> 00:47.380
But then, three years ago,

00:47.580 --> 00:50.050
Dr. Skinner
abruptly vanished without a trace.

00:50.380 --> 00:52.800
Not a soul knew where he had gone.

00:53.720 --> 00:54.920
And, as it turned out...

00:55.090 --> 00:59.260
Hapna was a huge trap
that he set upon the world.

01:10.110 --> 01:12.110
Hey, put on some music for me.

01:12.360 --> 01:14.070
What kind of music would you like?

01:14.570 --> 01:15.780
Let's see.

01:16.200 --> 01:17.530
Something that's got the vibe

01:17.700 --> 01:19.490
of a guy
who sold his soul to the devil.

01:19.660 --> 01:20.580
Or along those lines.

01:20.740 --> 01:22.080
That's the kind of song I want.

02:15.260 --> 02:16.670
Axel Gilberto.

02:17.090 --> 02:17.970
You've got a visitor.

02:22.180 --> 02:23.140
For me?

02:28.140 --> 02:29.850
You've only got ten minutes.

02:30.020 --> 02:30.770
We clear?

02:30.940 --> 02:33.230
Okay, that's plenty.

02:35.650 --> 02:37.320
Umm...

02:38.740 --> 02:40.530
Sorry, have we met before?

02:41.160 --> 02:42.780
We're complete strangers.

02:43.370 --> 02:44.530
This is the first time we've met.

02:45.080 --> 02:47.450
Every stranger who's taken
the time to visit me

02:47.620 --> 02:50.120
always turns out to be either
a lawyer or a hitman.

02:50.540 --> 02:53.380
Well, I suppose you might say
that I'm both.

02:53.540 --> 02:54.590
Huh?

02:54.750 --> 02:56.050
My name is Hersch.

02:56.550 --> 02:59.050
I've come here today
to ask for a favor.

02:59.630 --> 03:01.430
And depending on how you answer,

03:01.590 --> 03:04.430
I could free you
from your current situation.

03:05.640 --> 03:06.930
Free me, huh?

03:07.470 --> 03:09.140
Got any idea how long I'm serving?

03:09.600 --> 03:11.600
888 years.

03:11.770 --> 03:13.520
In other words, a life sentence.

03:14.270 --> 03:16.690
I know everything there
is to know about you.

03:16.860 --> 03:18.940
Your birth place, work history,

03:19.110 --> 03:20.700
medical history, shoe size,
you name it.

03:21.360 --> 03:22.990
What an honor.

03:23.160 --> 03:24.160
So, what's this favor of yours?

03:24.320 --> 03:25.620
I take it
you're familiar with Hapna.

03:25.780 --> 03:26.700
Of course.

03:26.870 --> 03:28.660
It's all the rage here in prison.

03:28.830 --> 03:30.410
What about Skinner's announcement?

03:30.660 --> 03:31.660
News to me.

03:31.870 --> 03:32.830
Let me show you.

03:33.000 --> 03:34.750
This clip was posted to every
video platform around the world

03:34.920 --> 03:36.710
about an hour ago.

03:36.960 --> 03:38.210
After vanishing
off the face of the Earth

03:38.380 --> 03:39.130
for the past three years,

03:39.340 --> 03:41.590
Dr. Skinner made his return.

03:42.970 --> 03:46.720
If you find yourself unable
to feel any pain at all,

03:47.140 --> 03:49.600
then that is no different
from being dead.

03:49.810 --> 03:51.180
While it is most unfortunate,

03:51.350 --> 03:55.440
humanity is basically dead now
due to its dependance upon Hapna.

03:55.940 --> 03:57.610
Furthermore,
humanity has become fixated

03:57.770 --> 03:59.610
on making short-term gains

03:59.780 --> 04:02.110
in a never-ending fight
amongst each other,

04:02.280 --> 04:05.620
which has irreparably destroyed
the environment of this planet

04:06.030 --> 04:08.530
and taken the lives
of countless people in the process.

04:08.740 --> 04:10.120
And so, as a scientist,

04:10.290 --> 04:12.120
I'm forced to come to the conclusion

04:12.330 --> 04:14.330
that this is the true nature
of human beings.

04:14.540 --> 04:15.830
No way...

04:16.710 --> 04:19.170
Can such atrocities be allowed?

04:19.340 --> 04:21.210
Shouldn't we, the human race,

04:21.380 --> 04:24.260
be held accountable
and face harsh punishment?

04:25.050 --> 04:26.970
The truth is,

04:27.140 --> 04:29.560
I did not develop Hapna
to act as a mere painkiller.

04:29.760 --> 04:32.140
It was engineered
to remain within the body

04:32.310 --> 04:35.060
and then mutate three years
after it was first taken

04:35.270 --> 04:37.060
into a toxin that is 100% lethal.

04:37.560 --> 04:39.070
And here we go...

04:39.270 --> 04:41.150
It is impossible for the toxin

04:41.320 --> 04:43.530
to be neutralized
or expelled from the body.

04:44.070 --> 04:46.200
I have no intention of playing God.

04:46.990 --> 04:49.200
Nor do I intend
to unilaterally decide

04:49.370 --> 04:51.290
what the fate of humanity will be.

04:52.080 --> 04:53.370
All I am doing...

04:53.540 --> 04:55.960
is serving as the Seventh Trumpeter.

04:56.120 --> 04:57.330
You gotta be kidding.

04:57.710 --> 05:01.170
In about thirty days, I estimate
the first people will die.

05:01.670 --> 05:05.050
But you should know
that I currently hold a cure.

05:05.220 --> 05:06.630
You have thirty days.

05:06.880 --> 05:08.850
If someone can find me
within that time...

05:09.640 --> 05:11.600
then humanity will survive.

05:12.270 --> 05:13.270
Excuse me, teach!

05:13.430 --> 05:14.230
Huh?

05:14.390 --> 05:16.140
Sorry to interrupt,
but I'm going home.

05:16.310 --> 05:18.190
And I don't think I'll ever be back.

05:18.350 --> 05:19.560
B-but why?

05:19.940 --> 05:21.320
I mean...

05:22.110 --> 05:24.440
What point is there in coming
to school anymore?

05:24.650 --> 05:28.570
Whether humanity is something
worth saving or not,

05:29.030 --> 05:31.950
is a decision that I leave
for all of you to decide.

05:33.700 --> 05:37.790
In the past, Skinner constantly
sought peace and equality for all.

05:37.960 --> 05:40.080
He was a real saint of a man.

05:40.670 --> 05:42.550
And now that he's back...

05:42.710 --> 05:44.460
he's turned into the devil?

05:47.260 --> 05:49.180
I want you to find him.

05:49.890 --> 05:52.640
That's the favor
I came here to ask you.

05:53.390 --> 05:54.560
Time's up.

05:57.600 --> 06:00.190
You've looked into everything
about me, yeah?

06:01.110 --> 06:02.360
Yes.

06:02.520 --> 06:04.190
Then you must already know...

06:04.400 --> 06:08.070
that I have a pretty bad habit
of breaking out of prison.

06:08.280 --> 06:09.860
Hurry it up.

06:10.320 --> 06:11.820
Why all the rush?

06:11.990 --> 06:13.490
Watch yourself, punk!

06:20.790 --> 06:21.960
Whoa there!

06:22.130 --> 06:23.000
No false moves.

06:27.920 --> 06:29.630
Wouldja mind taking these off me?

06:48.150 --> 06:49.240
Freeze!

07:07.050 --> 07:08.760
He fled to the third floor!
After him!

07:50.210 --> 07:52.380
Hey buddy! Let me out, too!

07:53.300 --> 07:54.340
You stupid little shit!

08:45.270 --> 08:45.980
Yes?

08:46.150 --> 08:48.310
He got away.
Bring the car around immediately.

08:48.810 --> 08:50.730
He flew away in the blink of an eye.

08:50.900 --> 08:53.240
Just like a bird
that was let out of its cage.

08:54.200 --> 08:55.360
Roger that.

09:01.830 --> 09:02.750
Leland!

09:02.910 --> 09:04.000
Oh, hey, Chris.

09:04.160 --> 09:05.160
Sup?

09:05.330 --> 09:07.290
Looks like someone's in a good mood.

09:07.460 --> 09:09.000
Huh, I do?

09:09.170 --> 09:10.380
Totally.

09:10.550 --> 09:13.260
Does humanity being doomed
really make you that happy?

09:13.420 --> 09:15.380
Nah, that's not why.

09:15.550 --> 09:16.720
Then what?

09:16.880 --> 09:17.930
It's just, ya know,

09:18.090 --> 09:19.470
I realized there's no point

09:19.640 --> 09:22.270
in forcing myself
to show up for school anymore.

09:22.430 --> 09:23.600
Know what I mean?

09:24.480 --> 09:25.640
You're such a kid!

09:25.810 --> 09:26.850
Ouch!

09:27.060 --> 09:27.900
What'd I say?

09:28.060 --> 09:29.110
Look, a kitty!

09:29.310 --> 09:31.070
Aww, it's so cute!

09:32.480 --> 09:34.360
I take that back.

09:37.320 --> 09:38.280
Eleina...

09:38.450 --> 09:40.830
Keep tabs on all police
communications and GPS.

09:40.990 --> 09:42.030
Roger.

09:44.330 --> 09:45.200
Unbelievable.

09:45.790 --> 09:47.420
What a pain in the ass.

09:47.580 --> 09:50.710
He could have been shot dead
by the police at this point.

09:50.920 --> 09:52.380
Highly unlikely.

09:53.920 --> 09:55.630
He's not that kind of man.

09:56.090 --> 09:59.140
It looks like the police
haven't found him yet, either.

10:00.140 --> 10:01.430
Understood.

10:01.600 --> 10:02.890
Keep monitoring them.

10:18.070 --> 10:19.280
Breaking news.

10:19.450 --> 10:21.780
After Dr. Skinner's shocking
statement earlier today,

10:21.950 --> 10:24.450
several cities have descended
into chaos.

10:24.620 --> 10:26.660
Full-on riots have broken
out in some places,

10:26.830 --> 10:29.330
while elsewhere,
people have begun lighting

10:29.500 --> 10:31.170
pharmaceutical companies on fire.

10:36.460 --> 10:37.420
My felllow citizens,

10:37.840 --> 10:40.050
I am urging you all
to please remain calm.

10:40.430 --> 10:43.180
We have already assembled
a team of experts

10:43.350 --> 10:47.060
who are doing everything they can
to swiftly develop a cure for Hapna.

10:50.350 --> 10:53.690
I can only assume Dr. Skinner
has lost his mind.

10:53.860 --> 10:56.860
I have no idea why he would do
something like this.

10:57.030 --> 10:58.610
Is it really true

10:58.780 --> 11:00.780
that all the people
who've taken Hapna can't be saved?

11:00.950 --> 11:02.110
I mean,
the government seems to think

11:02.280 --> 11:04.120
that it's possible for their people
to develop a cure.

11:04.580 --> 11:07.240
Thirty days
is simply not enough time.

11:07.410 --> 11:09.500
Even if a cure could be developed,

11:09.660 --> 11:12.120
it's likely that nobody
will be left alive when it's ready.

11:12.330 --> 11:13.960
In the wake of Skinner's video,

11:14.130 --> 11:15.340
pharmaceutical companies
have put an end

11:15.500 --> 11:17.670
to all Hapna sales across the board.

11:17.840 --> 11:19.760
And furthermore,
their representatives have announced

11:19.920 --> 11:21.840
an immediate recall of all product

11:22.010 --> 11:23.720
that is currently left
on the market.

11:23.930 --> 11:27.390
The end is nigh as Satan
calls forth Armageddon!

11:27.560 --> 11:31.350
We must come to terms with our fate
as there is no stopping it!

11:31.560 --> 11:33.980
A historical crash was reported
at the New York Stock Exchange today

11:34.150 --> 11:38.900
with the Dow Jones plunging
to its lowest numbers ever.

11:39.570 --> 11:42.360
This crash eclipses
even the infamous Black Monday.

11:50.710 --> 11:52.120
Hey there, young fella!

11:52.830 --> 11:54.420
What's with the getup?

11:55.130 --> 11:58.460
Is that prisoner look
a fashion trend these days or what?

11:58.630 --> 11:59.880
Oh, for sure! It's hip!

12:00.050 --> 12:03.470
Either that, or maybe you really are
a prison escapee?

12:03.630 --> 12:04.800
Yeah, right!

12:04.970 --> 12:06.720
Well, I guess
that would be ridiculous.

12:06.890 --> 12:10.310
Totally. I mean, what kind
of fugitive would be that stupid?

12:12.640 --> 12:14.350
Anyway, riots have been breaking out
all over the place.

12:14.520 --> 12:16.020
It's best you don't go wandering.

12:16.190 --> 12:17.060
I'll be careful.

12:17.230 --> 12:18.650
Get home quick now!

12:21.110 --> 12:22.190
Attention all units.

12:22.360 --> 12:24.660
It's been reported that an escapee
from Northport Correctional Facility

12:24.820 --> 12:27.070
has fled into the city.

12:27.280 --> 12:30.040
The suspect's name is
Axel Gilberto, age 23.

12:30.200 --> 12:31.830
Forwarding a picture to you now.

12:32.040 --> 12:33.040
That sonuva...!

12:58.020 --> 12:59.190
Well, shoot.

12:59.610 --> 13:03.280
It seems things are moving
even faster than we anticipated.

13:03.740 --> 13:06.700
Not to mention, they'll undoubtedly
move to destroy all the evidence

13:06.860 --> 13:09.780
if they get wind
that we're on their tracks.

13:10.450 --> 13:12.290
Secrecy and speed will be
of the utmost importance

13:12.450 --> 13:13.830
as we proceed
with this investigation.

13:14.000 --> 13:15.210
I understand.

13:15.580 --> 13:17.210
How is the analysis of Hapna going?

13:17.370 --> 13:20.920
We're working on it, but
it's proving to be a huge challenge.

13:21.500 --> 13:24.670
The thing is basically a true work
of art created by a genius.

13:24.840 --> 13:26.630
Developing a cure
in such a short period of time

13:26.800 --> 13:28.470
is going to be next to impossible.

13:28.930 --> 13:29.720
In other words,

13:29.890 --> 13:30.970
we're also at the point

13:31.140 --> 13:33.770
where the only viable option
is finding Dr. Skinner.

13:33.930 --> 13:35.230
Precisely.

13:35.770 --> 13:38.440
That last member of yours,
what happened with him?

13:38.600 --> 13:39.900
He got away.

13:40.270 --> 13:40.980
But...

13:41.520 --> 13:42.940
I promise that we'll get him.

13:43.150 --> 13:44.530
All right.

13:45.030 --> 13:49.320
You know, those people might
very well be our last hope.

14:14.140 --> 14:16.640
Fugitive Axel Gilberto.

14:16.810 --> 14:19.440
Stop resisting
and surrender immediately.

14:20.060 --> 14:21.900
Who, me? Bring it on!

14:23.730 --> 14:24.860
Hey!

14:35.910 --> 14:37.830
There he goes! That way!

15:04.570 --> 15:06.110
The target has shown up.

15:06.280 --> 15:07.150
He's at Central Station.

15:07.530 --> 15:09.110
Roger that. On my way.

15:09.280 --> 15:10.610
Weird.

15:11.110 --> 15:13.700
It looks like he's running somewhere
way off the roads...

15:13.910 --> 15:15.870
Okay. Time to greet our guest.

15:28.760 --> 15:30.260
Stop immediately!

15:30.470 --> 15:31.630
Axel Gilberto!

16:09.880 --> 16:12.300
So the dude just waltzed right
into Central Station?

16:12.470 --> 16:14.760
Yeah. It's about time he showed up.

16:22.100 --> 16:25.230
Eleina, can you run the data
and predict where he's headed to?

16:25.810 --> 16:26.900
Sure thing.

16:27.060 --> 16:28.730
I'll send it as soon as I can.

16:49.590 --> 16:51.050
The computer
has predicted his course.

16:51.210 --> 16:52.210
Forwarding the info now.

16:52.380 --> 16:53.090
Roger that.

16:53.630 --> 16:55.220
Chris, do you copy?

16:55.380 --> 16:56.800
You're about
to get some coordinates.

16:56.970 --> 16:58.010
Head there first.

16:58.180 --> 17:00.060
Then do what you can
to force him north-northwest.

17:00.430 --> 17:01.720
And my permission to open fire?

17:01.890 --> 17:03.020
Already taken care of.

17:03.180 --> 17:03.930
Oh, sweet!

17:04.520 --> 17:06.230
Just try not to hit anyone!

17:06.770 --> 17:08.520
And don't damage any property!

17:45.350 --> 17:46.440
Stop immediately!

17:46.600 --> 17:48.020
Axel Gilberto!

18:25.390 --> 18:26.930
- Back me up.
- You got it!

18:47.200 --> 18:48.410
Freeze!

18:49.250 --> 18:50.500
Show's over.

18:50.670 --> 18:52.380
Put your hands in the air.

18:53.790 --> 18:54.960
Oh, I get it.

18:55.130 --> 18:58.010
You cut off my route
to get me to come to this building.

18:58.800 --> 19:00.220
And it worked perfectly.

19:00.800 --> 19:01.840
Hold up.

19:02.010 --> 19:04.760
I don't get to see the face
of the guy who's gonna kill me?

19:04.930 --> 19:06.770
Can I at least get a name?

19:06.930 --> 19:08.310
Douglas Hadine.

19:08.480 --> 19:10.230
Do me a solid
and put this on my gravestone:

19:10.730 --> 19:12.480
"Here lies a helpless man

19:12.650 --> 19:14.940
shot and killed from behind
by the cowardly Doug Whatshisface."

19:16.230 --> 19:17.650
I'm not falling for that.

19:17.820 --> 19:19.320
You're being provocative on purpose

19:19.530 --> 19:21.780
so that you can lure me
into a close quarters fight.

19:22.910 --> 19:24.070
You got me.

19:24.280 --> 19:26.290
In any case,
this is the end of the line for you.

19:26.450 --> 19:28.200
Seeing as how humans
weren't built to fly.

19:28.370 --> 19:29.370
Normally speaking.

19:29.540 --> 19:31.790
Only boring losers
care about being normal.

19:32.290 --> 19:33.830
You wanna test that theory?

20:16.840 --> 20:18.750
Hey, Mister Daredevil!
Look over here!

20:21.630 --> 20:22.720
You are so badass!

20:22.880 --> 20:23.840
Oh my god!

20:24.010 --> 20:25.300
I think that was, like,
the most awesome

20:25.470 --> 20:26.890
street performance I've ever seen!

20:27.050 --> 20:28.390
Uh, well...

20:29.060 --> 20:31.060
I was actually just running
from a dude...

20:31.230 --> 20:32.100
So, hey...

20:32.310 --> 20:34.020
Would you mind if we took...

20:34.190 --> 20:34.850
a selfie together?

20:35.060 --> 20:36.480
Huh? Well, actually I...

20:36.650 --> 20:38.650
Sweet! Okay!

20:38.820 --> 20:40.860
Ready? 3, 2, 1...

20:41.070 --> 20:42.110
Smile!

21:30.530 --> 21:31.990
The hell is this thing?

21:46.590 --> 21:49.510
Oh! He's finally awake!

21:49.970 --> 21:50.930
Wanna know what's crazy?

21:51.100 --> 21:52.890
You were out cold
for pretty much an entire day!

21:53.470 --> 21:57.440
Since you wouldn't wake up at all,
we kinda thought you were dead.

21:57.600 --> 21:58.770
I recognize you guys.

21:58.940 --> 22:00.400
You were in my dream...

22:00.560 --> 22:01.980
That wasn't a dream.

22:03.280 --> 22:04.990
We finally meet again.

22:06.110 --> 22:09.570
I seriously have no idea
what the hell is going on here.

22:09.740 --> 22:11.620
Who even are you people?

22:12.280 --> 22:13.620
We are...

22:13.790 --> 22:14.490
Lazarus.

22:15.410 --> 22:18.460
Welcome aboard, Axel Gilberto.

22:19.620 --> 22:20.920
Huh...?
